CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_Location "Identifies which tire is associated with the parametric data in this PGN.
The low order 4 bits represent a position number, counting left to right when facing in the direction of normal vehicle travel (forward).
The high order 4 bits represent a ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_Press "Pressure at which air is contained in cavity formed by tire and rim.";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_Temp "Temperature at the surface of the tire sidewall.";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_Stat "Indicates the status of the tire.";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_ExtendTirePressSupport "Defines the choice of using the tire pressure (PGN 65268) or Extended Tire Pressure (PGN 64578). The state value '01' indicates the extended tire pressure SPN is used for the pressure data. Any other value indicates the extended tire pressure SPN is ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_AirLeakageRate "The pressure loss rate of a tire.";
CM_ SG_ 2566845491 TIRE1_PressThresholdDetect "Signal indicating the pressure level of the tire.";
CM_ SG_ 2566668851 TIRE2_Location "Identifies which tire is associated with the parametric data in PGN 64578. Refer to SPN 929 for further details and examples. The low order 4 bits represent a position number, counting left to right when facing in the direction of normal vehicle .Examples: Tire pressure for location 0x00 would be left front tire.Tire pressure for location 0x23 would be right outside rear rear on a 3-axle tractor with dual axle per side (3rd axle, 4thtire).";
CM_ SG_ 2566668851 TIRE2_PressExtendRange "Pressure at which air is contained in cavity formed by tire and rim. See SPN 241 for alternate tire pressure with a lower range and coarser resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2566668851 TIRE2_ReqTirePress "The required tire pressure at which air is contained in cavity formed by tire and rim.

This pressure of the tire is compensated to meet the specific physical environmental conditions (temperature) of the vehicle.";
CM_ SG_ 2566897971 TIRE3_TireLocation "Identifies which tire is associated with the parametric data in this PGN.The low order 4 bits represent a Postn number, counting left to right when facing in the direction of normal Vhcltravel (forward).The high order 4 bits represent a Postn number, counting front to back on the Vhcl.The value 0xFF indicates not available.It is recommended that output devices add 1 to the Postn number (range 1 to 15, not 0 to 14) for use by Drvs andservice technicians.Examples: Tire Press for location 0x00 would be left front tire.Tire Press for location 0x23 would be right outside rear rear on a 3-axle tractor with dual axle per side (3rd axle,4th tire).";
CM_ SG_ 2566897971 TIRE3_TireSensorMatchStat "Identifies whether the tire sensor is matched or not.";
CM_ SG_ 2566897971 TIRE3_TireSensorSelfLearningStat "Identifies the self learning Sts of tire sensor.";
CM_ SG_ 2566897971 TIRE3_TireSensorElectricalFault "Indicates the Sts of electrical fault on the tire sensor.";
CM_ SG_ 2566897971 TIRE3_TireTemThresholdDetection "Signal indicating the Temperature level of the tire. The levels defined represent different temperatureconditions of the tire.";
