CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_LDWSwitchStat "Signal which indicates LDW Swch Sts. It is the nonlocking Swch, the signal value should be 1 during the Swch be pressed
LDW开关状态，自复位开关";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_FCWSwitchStat "Signal which indicates FCW Swch Sts. It is the nonlocking Swch, the signal value should be 1during the Swch be pressed";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_ReverseGearSwitch "Indicates the Sts of reverse gear Swch.";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_RearWorkLampSwitch "Indicates the Sts of rear work lamp Swch";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_SleepAreaLightSwitch "Swch signal which indicates the Sts of “sleep area light“. It is the nonlocking Swch, the signal valueshould be 1 during the Swch be pressed.";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_IndoorLightSwitch "Swch signal which indicates the Sts of “indoor light“. It is the nonlocking Swch, the signal valueshould be 1 during the Swch be pressed";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_HornSwitch "Swch signal which indicates the Sts of menu “horn“. It is the nonlocking Swch, the signal valueshould be 1 during the Swch be pressed.";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_HornSelectionSwitch "indicate the selected Postn of the horn selection Swch";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_CabDoorWarnOFFSwitch "indicate the cab door Warn off Swch";
CM_ SG_ 2566849057 SC_AutoLightCtrlSwitch "indicate the auto light Ctrl Swch";
CM_ SG_ 2566848801 BCU_IgnitionPstn "点火开关状态";
CM_ SG_ 2566848801 BCU_DriverSeatBeltAlert "Indicates whether the Drv's side safety belt is not fastened to alarm";
CM_ SG_ 2566848801 BCU_PassengerSeatBeltAlert "Indicates whether the Pasgr side safety belt is not fastened to alarm";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_HCUSysStat "表示整车控制器系统工作状态：";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_ReadyToDriveStat "表示整车运行准备就绪状态。";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_PermitCharge "Indicates whether Charge is allowed.";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_EnduranceMileage "Indicates the mileage, used for the display of the instrument.The actual physical value range is 0km-500km";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_SleepCmd "Indicates the sleep Cmd sent by HCU. After receiving it, the receiving node realizes the sleep wakefunction according to the network sleep wake strategy.";
CM_ SG_ 2566849575 HCU_BMS_HighVoltSysFailStat "Indicates High Voltage System Failure Status.
Level 1 failure: alarm；
Level 2 failure: limit；
Level 2 failure: Shut Down";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattVolt "Represents the power Battary Voltage.The actual physical value ranges from 0V to 1000V.";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattCurrent "Represents power Batt Curr, Ngtv value represents charge, Pstv value represents discharge.";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattSOC "Represents the remaining charge of the power Batt";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattSysStat "Represents the Current working Status of the power Battary System.The first alarm is a general fault;The secondary alarm is a serious fault; (limited power)Three-level alarm for emergency failure; (electricity)";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattChargeReq "Indicates whether there is a charge Req.000：No charge Req before charge ready001：When the Chrg is ready, send the Chrg Req010：Req Chrg stop in case of recoverable fault (reservation)011：Unrecoverable fault occurs, Req for Chrg (reservation)";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattChargeStat "Represents the Current Charge Status of the power Battary";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_PowerBattHeatStat "Indicates the heating Sts of the power Batt";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_MsgCounter "The message counter is used to detect situations where the transmitting ECU malfunction repeats thesame frame all the time. The receiver of the formation may use the counter parameter to detect thissituation. The transmitting device will increase the message counter in every cycle. The message counterwill count from 0 to 7 and then wrap. The values 0x8 thru 0xE are SAE reserved and should be ignoredby the receiver.Value 0xF (all bits set to 1) will indicate that the message counter is not available. Forcompatibility purposes, TSC1 should also be honored if the message counter is not available from thetransmitting device.";
CM_ SG_ 2566862323 BMS1_MsgChecksum "Message checksum is used to verify the signal transmission path from the sending device to the receivingdevice. The checksum is the sum of the following data: the sum of the message ID from high to lowbytes, the first seven bytes of the data area, and the message counter. The checksum calculation formulais as follows:Checksum = (byte 1 + byte 2 + byte 3 + byte 4 + byte 5 + byte 6 + byte 7 + message counter & 0x0F +message ID low byte + message ID medium low byte + message ID high byte + message ID high byte)Checksum = ((checksum >> 4) + checksum) & 0x0FThe checksum value 0x0F indicates that the checksum is not available.";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_BMSMainNgtvCoilDrvStat "BMS primary negative coil drive state";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_PowerBattSOH "Represents the Batt health Sts, and the value range is 0-100%.";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_MainNgtvRelayDisconnectReq "Main Negative Relay Disconnect Request
Represents that BMS sends the main-Ngtv relay disconnect Req to HCU:
When the HCU has no response, the BMS will actively disconnect the main-Ngtv relay after 30s";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_MainNgtvRelayStat "Represents the state of the main-negative relay:";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_BattPackHeatCtrlCmdPstv "Indicates the Battery Pack Heating Positive Relay Control Command Signal";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_BattPackHeatCtrlCmdNgtv "Indicates the Battery Pack Heating Negative Relay Control Command Signal";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_ChargePlugConnectionStat "ndicates the connection Sts of the Chrg plug.If the dual gun is charged, the signal indicates cc2-1.";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_ChargePlug2ConnectionStat "Represents the connection Sts of Chrg plug 2. The signal can only be obtained when the dual gun ischarged (cc2-2)";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_ChargeRelayStatPstv "Represents the state of charging positive relay.";
CM_ SG_ 2566863603 BMS5_ChargeRelayStatNgtv "Represents the state of charging positive relay.";
